Cybersecurity Agent — Modern Agent Workspace UI Specification
1. Core design direction
Redesign the existing Tkinter dashboard into a clean, minimal, professional AI-agent workspace inspired by the interaction model of modern coding agents such as Codex, Claude Code, Kilo Code, OpenCode, and similar agentic development environments.

The current application feels like a legacy SOC/admin dashboard because it exposes almost every capability as a button.

The new UI should instead feel like:

"I am talking to an autonomous cybersecurity agent, and I can see what it is doing."

The user should not need to understand which tool, agent, workflow, database function, or subsystem needs to be called.

The agent should be the primary interface.

Tools and subsystems should appear as contextual execution details.

